    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-71448: the normals have cross product (1,1,1), so they are not parallel and only III is true. q-71468: the normals are scalar multiples, but the planes have different offsets, so they are distinct parallel planes and only I is true. q-128308: expansion along the first row gives 35-3-27=5. q-70974: (3,0,4)×(1,-1,1)=(4,1,-3), perpendicular to both plane directions. q-71040: D-C=(-4,1,3), independent of (0,1,1); the selected parametrization passes through both points and has the required direction. q-72094: the sum factors as (1+2+3)(1+2)=18. q-72396: the inner sums are -3,0,3, totaling 0. q-149673: linearity gives 3(50)+2(20)=190. q-149675: there are 80 constant terms, giving 80+25+2(20)=145. q-149620: separation gives (12-10)(5+20)=50. q-149736: separation gives (35-30)(20+45)=325. q-332550: the particular solution -x²+4x-7 has derivative -2x+4, and their sum is -x²+2x-3; adding Ae^(-x) gives the general solution. q-33662: the point corresponds to t=1, where the velocity is (1,8,4) with norm 9. q-127280: the product rule gives velocity (2,-4,5) with norm 3√5; rationalizing the normalized components gives the selected answer. q-78254 and q-116085: reading the translations in standard hyperbola form gives centers (-4,2) and (4,-1), respectively. Each MA evidence entry is a contiguous verbatim substring of that question's captured solution. No grade evidence was supplied; confirmation rests on the worked solutions and independent mathematics.",
